From 165b483b610de250bf662b1043dbc299e765b90a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PathOps <noreply@pathops.dev>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:10:35 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] delegation: operation-scoped delegated authorization (PAR,
 RAR, signed plans)

Add the opt-in "delegation" configuration for PathOps operation-scoped human
delegated authorization (PathOps Decision 0050):

- a pushed authorization request endpoint (RFC 9126, /par) for configured
  public plan clients. The request carries RAR authorization_details
  (RFC 9396) and a PathOps Authorization Plan: an EdDSA JWS by a configured
  delegate that binds subject, operation, Application/Run, client, redirect
  URI, PKCE challenge, tool audiences and the exact details. Dex verifies the
  signature and requires the pushed details to equal the plan's in canonical
  JSON; request_uri values are short-lived and single-use;
- authorization_details and the plan are refused on the front channel;
- a per-operation consent screen (delegation.html) that skipApprovalScreen
  and stored consents never bypass; the authenticated user must be the
  plan's subject;
- an operation grant stored in the user's UserIdentity (reserved Consents
  key), approved on consent and activated only when the code is redeemed
  with the plan's PKCE verifier; the code response carries the approved
  authorization_details;
- a delegated derivation for the plan's delegate, an authenticated
  confidential client: an RFC 8693 token exchange whose subject is the
  operation grant handle (never a user token) mints a token with one
  audience, a subset of the approved details, azp = the delegate, a lifetime
  of at most tokensValidFor and never beyond the grant, and no refresh token;
- discovery advertises the PAR endpoint and the detail types.

The delegation state rides on a new AuthRequest/AuthCode field kept by the
kubernetes and memory storages; Dex refuses delegation with other storages.
Without the configuration, behavior is unchanged.
